        {
          "type": "response_end",
          "response": {
            "text": "Alberto builds agents with a strong focus on measurement and human oversight:\n\n- **Offline evals before shipping:** His site's agent records eval cases against a real model and replays them in CI with no network. A stale recording or an off-topic leak fails the build.\n- **Graded autonomy with a human in the loop:** His deployed Fraud Detection Agent recommends approve, reject or request-info, and a human admin decides. It auto-approves only on evidence verified in code, and web sources can hold a decision back but never approve it.\n- **Regression cases from failures:** Each real failure becomes a new regression case.\n- **Cost and limits tracked:** The site's agent has a per-request token budget, per-IP rate limits and a monthly spend cap. Eval reports show tokens, latency and cost per case.\n- **Changes measured run over run:** Every eval run is logged to a history, so changes to prompts, tools or content show up against the previous run.\n\nStack examples: TypeScript, Claude, MCP, PostgreSQL and GCP. If you want, I can go into the Fraud Detection Agent's results or the portfolio agent's source code.",
