              "type": "response_end",
              "response": {
                "text": "Alberto builds agents with a strong focus on evaluation, human oversight and cost control:\n\n- **Offline evals before shipping:** Agents are tested against recorded eval cases that replay in CI with no model or network. A stale recording or an off-topic leak fails the build. Real failures become new regression cases.\n- **Graded autonomy with a human in the loop:** His deployed fraud detection agent recommends approve, reject or request-info, and a human admin makes the final call. It auto-approves only on evidence verified in code, and web sources can hold a decision back but never approve it.\n- **Cost and limits tracked:** The site's agent has a per-request token budget, per-IP rate limits and a monthly spend cap. Each eval report shows mean tokens, latency and cost per case.\n- **Changes measured run over run:** Each eval run is logged to a history, so changes to prompts, tools or content show up against the previous run.\n\nStack: TypeScript, Claude, MCP, PostgreSQL and GCP. For example, the fraud agent went from 68% to 92% accuracy on its reference set after switching to Claude Haiku, at about $0.002 per review. Want details on any of these projects?",
